 "notes": [
  "All candidate names and parties come from the official SOS Ballot Certification Report for the 2026 November General Election (certified Aug 28, 2026 by Deputy Secretary of State Dave Nelson), which lists names in capitals with party codes REP/DEM/LIB/GRE/IND; names here are converted to mixed case. Party codes mapped to Republican/Democratic/Libertarian/Green/Independent.",
  "Candidate order within each race follows the certification (Republican, Democratic, then third parties); actual ballot party order is set by Election Code sec. 52.091 (the governor's party in the last gubernatorial election goes first).",
  "Write-in candidates are excluded (e.g., U.S. Senate, Governor, Lt. Governor, CD 27, CD 33 have declared write-ins per Ballotpedia/Green Papers).",
  "Statewide judicial offices include the Supreme Court (Chief Justice, Places 2 [unexpired term], 7, 8), Court of Criminal Appeals (Places 3, 4, 9), and the 15th Court of Appeals, which is elected statewide. The State Board of Education is district-based and not included.",
  "U.S. Senate seat is Class 2 (Cornyn), open after Ken Paxton defeated Cornyn in the May 26, 2026 Republican runoff.",
  "Districts are the 2025 mid-decade redistricting map; several incumbents run in new districts.",
  "Texas Election Code sec. 41.031: polls open 7 a.m. to 7 p.m.; voters in line at 7 p.m. may still vote. DST ends Nov 1, so 7 p.m. CST = 01:00 UTC and 7 p.m. MST = 02:00 UTC on Nov 4."
 ],
 "unconfirmed": [
  "Whether any certified candidate withdrew, died, or was declared ineligible after the Aug 28, 2026 certification (names would generally remain on the ballot); no later SOS amendment to the certification was found.",
  "Exact mixed-case spelling as printed on county ballots (the certification is all caps): e.g., 'DiBianca', 'McCormick', 'McDonough', 'McMenemy', 'Dashaun', 'Heli' quotes.",
  "Whether the small part of Culberson County that observes Mountain Time affects the latest close; the 02:00 UTC figure assumes Mountain Time counties (El Paso, Hudspeth) close at 7 p.m. MST, which is the latest anywhere either way.",
  "Effective date: no measures exist, so measureEffective is a notional placeholder (end of the state canvass window), not a real effective date."
 ]
